$\begin{align}
y^3-3y^2&=11-2x
\\\\
3y^2\cdot\dfrac{dy}{dt}-6y\cdot\dfrac{dy}{dt}&=-2\cdot\dfrac{dx}{dt}
\\\\
(3y^2-6y)\cdot\dfrac{dy}{dt}&=-2\cdot\dfrac{dx}{dt}
\end{align}$

We are given that $\dfrac{dx}{dt}=4$, and we want to find $\dfrac{dy}{dt}$ when $y=-2$.

Let's plug $\blueD{y=-2}$ and $\goldD{\dfrac{dx}{dt}=4}$ into the equation we obtained:

$\begin{align}
(3\blueD{y}^2-6\blueD{y})\cdot\dfrac{dy}{dt}&=-2\cdot\goldD{\dfrac{dx}{dt}}
\\\\
(3(\blueD{-2})^2-6(\blueD{-2}))\cdot\dfrac{dy}{dt}&=-2\cdot\goldD{4}
\\\\
24\cdot\dfrac{dy}{dt}&=-8
\\\\
\dfrac{dy}{dt}&=-\dfrac{1}{3}
\end{align}$
